[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-SERVER
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
server.py is one stdlib threaded HTTP server: GET and HEAD only, an
allowlisted static surface, and three JSON routes -- /api/health (the daemon's
describe), /api/graph (the sdoc-board/2 snapshot) and /api/rows (the
sdoc-perspective/2 tables). source.py's DaemonSource holds the adapted
payloads keyed by daemon generation and re-exports only when describe reports
movement, so a repeat request costs no export. A NoDaemon refusal becomes HTTP
503 with the remedy in the body; any other daemon error is a 502. The process
imports nothing from strictdoc, so ./serve runs under any python3, and
devenv.nix declares it as processes.board -- `devenv up board`, `-d`, and
`devenv processes down`, the same lifecycle as processes.scribe and
independent of it.

source.py also builds the snapshot's semantics key by calling
sdoc_semantics.build_payload over the same parsed grammar the adapter already
reads. sdoc_semantics is standard-library-only, so its import can fail only
when that package is off the path; a failure becomes a named refusal inside
the payload rather than a missing key or a dead process. The extractor the
adapter asks for KIND words is the one real optional dependency because it
needs tree_sitter and a compiled grammar, and it degrades the same way. Thus
any python3 still serves the base app, while either absent enrichment says so
explicitly.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 8823edf1 and 46cd3cf1: the static allowlist
grew grammar-groups.json and fsm.js, and source.py gained the semantics
payload. The three JSON routes are unchanged -- semantics rides inside
/api/graph rather than on a fourth route.

Updated 2026-09-08 for commit 8b936c3c: the allowlist grew two more entries,
/assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-api.js and /assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-worker.min.js,
and they are the only ones not backed by a file in this directory -- server.py
resolves them against the Nix store path in SDOC_BOARD_ELKJS_DIR and refuses
to start when that variable is unset or does not hold both files. SDOC_BOARD_ELKJS_DIR is the one environment variable the process requires beyond its interpreter;
MECH-SDOC-BOARD-LAYOUT owns the delivery. Still three JSON routes.

Corrected 2026-09-10: sdoc_semantics has been standard-library-only since the transitions dependency was removed. The current server still executes python3 from PATH and still parses grammar.sgra locally; the planned pinned interpreter and daemon-served grammar revisions are deferred until those code paths land.
<<<
